WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.258
Previously on Supernatural.

00:00:05.066 --> 00:00:08.636
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:09.986 --> 00:00:11.569
Mary! No!

00:00:13.335 --> 00:00:14.478
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:15.607 --> 00:00:17.163
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:19.136 --> 00:00:20.539
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:21.228 --> 00:00:22.729
I can't do this alone.

00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:29.695
We got work to do.

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:31.334
This is dad's single

00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:32.655
Most valuable possession.

00:00:32.682 --> 00:00:34.995
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:35.037 --> 00:00:37.011
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:37.052 --> 00:00:38.359
You know, saving people,

00:00:38.388 --> 00:00:39.475
Hunting things...

00:00:39.516 --> 00:00:40.397
Family business.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:40.927
No.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.345
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:00:42.386 --> 00:00:43.860
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:43.914 --> 00:00:45.769
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:47.584 --> 00:00:48.981
Yeah, I know.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:05.467
Morning, daddy.

00:01:05.529 --> 00:01:06.911
Morning, sweetheart.

00:01:09.145 --> 00:01:11.421
All these workouts, Soph, I don't know.

00:01:11.547 --> 00:01:13.353
Guys don't like buff girls.

00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:16.325
Yeah, well, girls don't like
guys who still live at home.

00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:24.665
Be careful.

00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:25.827
I will.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:04.029
Can I get you anything else?

00:03:07.247 --> 00:03:08.818
Just the check, please.

00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:09.826
Okay.

00:03:14.615 --> 00:03:17.881
You know, Sam, we are allowed
to have fun once in a while.

00:03:20.722 --> 00:03:21.822
That's fun.

00:03:26.174 --> 00:03:28.199
Here, take a look at
this. I think I got one.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.146
Lake Manitoc, Wisconsin.

00:03:30.318 --> 00:03:31.951
Last week, Sophie Carlton,

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.279
18, walks into the lake,

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.551
Doesn't walk out.

00:03:35.598 --> 00:03:37.278
Authorities dragged the water.

00:03:37.356 --> 00:03:38.251
Nothing.

00:03:38.424 --> 00:03:41.301
Sophie Carlton is the third
Lake Manitoc drowning this year.

00:03:41.427 --> 00:03:43.201
None of the other
bodies were found, either

00:03:43.342 --> 00:03:44.488
They had a funeral two days ago.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.163
A funeral?

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:47.250
Yes, they buried an empty coffin.

00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:50.398
For closure or whatever.

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:51.716
Closure?

00:03:52.862 --> 00:03:53.804
What closure?

00:03:54.008 --> 00:03:55.782
People don't just disappear, Dean.

00:03:56.017 --> 00:03:57.980
Other people just stop looking for them.

00:03:59.774 --> 00:04:00.872
Something you want to say to me?

00:04:00.908 --> 00:04:03.656
The trail for dad. It's getting colder.

00:04:03.781 --> 00:04:04.362
Every day.

00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:06.418
What are we supposed
to do? I don't know.

00:04:06.638 --> 00:04:07.470
Something.

00:04:07.611 --> 00:04:08.757
Anything. No one.

00:04:08.967 --> 00:04:10.191
I'm sick of this attitude.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.106
You don't think I want to
find dad as much as you do?

00:04:12.137 --> 00:04:12.922
Yeah, I know you do it.

00:04:12.953 --> 00:04:15.638
I'm the one that's been with him every
single day for the past two years.

00:04:15.748 --> 00:04:17.946
While you've been off to
college going to pep rallies.

00:04:18.087 --> 00:04:19.280
We will find dad,

00:04:19.343 --> 00:04:21.556
But until then, we're
gonna kill everything bad,

00:04:21.697 --> 00:04:23.236
Between here and there.

00:04:24.052 --> 00:04:25.104
Okay?

00:04:31.785 --> 00:04:33.762
All right, Lake Manitoc.

00:04:34.469 --> 00:04:34.845
Hey.

00:04:34.955 --> 00:04:35.395
Huh?

00:04:35.442 --> 00:04:36.243
How far?

00:04:57.614 --> 00:04:58.477
Will Carlton?

00:04:58.854 --> 00:04:59.545
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:00.769
I'm agent Ford.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.300
This is agent Hamill.

00:05:02.786 --> 00:05:04.577
We're with the U.S. Wildlife service.

00:05:11.903 --> 00:05:13.787
She was about 100 yards out.

00:05:15.419 --> 00:05:16.518
That's where she got dragged down.

00:05:16.581 --> 00:05:17.931
And you're sure she didn't just drown?

00:05:17.963 --> 00:05:18.402
Yeah.

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:20.160
She was a varsity swimmer.

00:05:20.254 --> 00:05:22.043
She practically grew up in that lake.

00:05:23.173 --> 00:05:25.356
She's as safe out there
as in her own bathtub.

00:05:25.937 --> 00:05:27.208
So no splashing,

00:05:27.302 --> 00:05:28.417
No signs of distress?

00:05:28.464 --> 00:05:29.625
No, that's what I'm telling you.

00:05:29.803 --> 00:05:31.953
Did you see any shadows in the water,

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:33.649
Maybe,

00:05:33.852 --> 00:05:36.301
Some dark shape breach the surface?

00:05:36.348 --> 00:05:38.373
No, again, she was really far out there.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.225
You ever see any strange
tracks by the shoreline?

00:05:40.256 --> 00:05:41.167
No, never.

00:05:41.276 --> 00:05:42.093
Why?

00:05:42.219 --> 00:05:43.569
What do you think's out there?

00:05:44.025 --> 00:05:46.316
We'll let you know as soon as we do.

00:05:48.561 --> 00:05:50.068
What about your father?

00:05:50.304 --> 00:05:51.764
Can we talk to him?

00:05:53.841 --> 00:05:54.485
Look.

00:05:54.594 --> 00:05:56.085
If you don't mind, I mean,

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.818
He didn't see anything, and
he's kind of been through a lot.

00:05:59.712 --> 00:06:00.968
We understand.

00:06:07.344 --> 00:06:08.292
Now, I'm sorry, but,

00:06:08.318 --> 00:06:12.531
Why does the wildlife service
care about an accidental drowning?

00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:14.016
You sure it's accidental?

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.266
Will Carlton saw
something grab his sister.

00:06:16.832 --> 00:06:17.977
Like what?

00:06:18.417 --> 00:06:19.452
Here, sit, please.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.546
There are no indigenous
carnivores in that lake.

00:06:22.789 --> 00:06:25.450
There's nothing even big
enough to pull down a person,

00:06:25.536 --> 00:06:27.388
Unless it was the Loch Ness monster.

00:06:28.244 --> 00:06:29.704
Yeah, right.

00:06:29.829 --> 00:06:33.911
Will Carlton was traumatized, and
sometimes the mind plays tricks.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.203
Still,

00:06:35.736 --> 00:06:39.315
We dragged that entire lake.
We even ran a sonar sweep,

00:06:39.745 --> 00:06:42.146
Just to be sure, and there
was nothing down there.

00:06:42.225 --> 00:06:44.281
That's weird, though.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.322
That's the third missing body this year.

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.504
I know.

00:06:48.163 --> 00:06:49.953
These are people from my town.

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:51.617
These are people I care about.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:52.543
I know.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:54.981
Anyway . . .

00:06:56.693 --> 00:06:57.948
All this.

00:06:59.283 --> 00:07:01.167
It won't be a problem much longer.

00:07:01.747 --> 00:07:02.800
What do you mean?

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:05.130
Well, the dam, of course.

00:07:06.448 --> 00:07:07.641
Of course.

00:07:07.908 --> 00:07:08.818
The dam.

00:07:09.132 --> 00:07:10.169
It's, uh...

00:07:11.613 --> 00:07:12.460
It sprung a leak.

00:07:12.539 --> 00:07:13.669
It's falling apart,

00:07:14.282 --> 00:07:17.049
And the feds won't give
us the grant to repair it,

00:07:17.112 --> 00:07:18.808
So they've opened the spillway.

00:07:19.435 --> 00:07:21.225
In another six months,

00:07:21.837 --> 00:07:23.266
There won't be much of a lake.

00:07:23.517 --> 00:07:25.091
There won't be much of a town, either,

00:07:25.232 --> 00:07:26.300
But as federal wildlife,

00:07:26.426 --> 00:07:27.823
You already knew that.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:29.361
Exactly.

00:07:30.021 --> 00:07:31.967
Sorry, am I interrupting?

00:07:32.506 --> 00:07:33.730
I think come back later.

00:07:33.872 --> 00:07:35.880
Gentlemen, this is my daughter.

00:07:36.305 --> 00:07:37.498
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:37.843 --> 00:07:38.769
I'm Dean.

00:07:39.146 --> 00:07:40.543
Andrea Bar. Hi.

00:07:40.748 --> 00:07:41.171
Hi.

00:07:41.396 --> 00:07:42.918
They're from the wildlife service,

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.787
About the lake.

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.302
Oh, hey, there.

00:07:50.589 --> 00:07:51.546
What's your name?

00:07:57.889 --> 00:07:59.223
His name is Lucas.

00:08:02.108 --> 00:08:02.987
Is he okay?

00:08:03.065 --> 00:08:04.698
My grandson's been through a lot.

00:08:05.624 --> 00:08:06.943
We all have.

00:08:07.822 --> 00:08:08.638
Well,

00:08:09.413 --> 00:08:10.982
If there's anything
else I can do for you,

00:08:10.999 --> 00:08:12.067
Please, let me know.

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:12.945
Thanks.

00:08:13.829 --> 00:08:15.539
You know, now that you mentioned it,

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:18.884
Could you point us in the direction
of a reasonably priced motel?

00:08:19.076 --> 00:08:21.793
Lake front motel, go around
the corner, it's two blocks up.

00:08:21.856 --> 00:08:22.577
Two.

00:08:23.205 --> 00:08:24.210
Would you mind showing us?

00:08:25.607 --> 00:08:27.287
You want me to walk you two blocks?

00:08:27.365 --> 00:08:28.653
Not if it's any trouble.

00:08:29.264 --> 00:08:31.132
I'm headed that way anyway.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:34.335
I'll be back to pick up lucas at 3:00.

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.171
We'll go to the park, okay, sweetie?

00:08:40.132 --> 00:08:41.247
Thanks again.

00:08:42.315 --> 00:08:43.539
So, cute kid.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:44.481
Thanks.

00:08:46.637 --> 00:08:48.113
Kids are the best, huh?

00:08:51.932 --> 00:08:53.267
There it is.

00:08:53.879 --> 00:08:55.386
Like I said, two blocks.

00:08:55.464 --> 00:08:56.234
Thanks.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.499
Must be hard with your
sense of direction,

00:08:59.876 --> 00:09:02.780
Never being able to find your
way to a decent pickup line.

00:09:04.323 --> 00:09:05.563
Enjoy your stay.

00:09:07.432 --> 00:09:08.562
"Kids are the best"?

00:09:09.163 --> 00:09:11.016
You don't even like kids. I love kids.

00:09:11.079 --> 00:09:13.324
Name three children that you even know.

00:09:20.073 --> 00:09:21.141
I'm thinking.

00:09:21.549 --> 00:09:24.061
So there's the three
drowning victims this year.

00:09:24.092 --> 00:09:25.034
And before that?

00:09:25.176 --> 00:09:27.954
Yeah, six more,

00:09:27.985 --> 00:09:29.570
Spread outover the past 35 years.

00:09:29.712 --> 00:09:31.517
Those bodies were
never recovered, either.

00:09:32.129 --> 00:09:33.621
If there is something out there,

00:09:33.772 --> 00:09:34.730
It's picking up its pace.

00:09:34.792 --> 00:09:36.315
So we got a lake monster on a binge?

00:09:36.362 --> 00:09:39.062
This whole lake monster
theory, it just bugs me.

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:40.177
Why?

00:09:40.716 --> 00:09:42.474
Loch Ness, lake Champlain

00:09:42.505 --> 00:09:45.080
There are literally hundreds
of eyewitness accounts,

00:09:45.127 --> 00:09:46.995
But here, almost nothing.

00:09:47.324 --> 00:09:48.609
Whatever it is out there,

00:09:48.911 --> 00:09:50.276
Noone's living to talk about it.

00:09:50.528 --> 00:09:51.799
Wait, Bar,

00:09:52.055 --> 00:09:53.940
Christopher Bar, where have
I heard that name before?

00:09:53.971 --> 00:09:56.593
Christopher Bar, the victim in may.

00:09:58.256 --> 00:10:00.172
Christopher Bar was Andrea's husband,

00:10:00.468 --> 00:10:01.912
Lucas' father.

00:10:02.371 --> 00:10:03.251
Apparently,

00:10:03.486 --> 00:10:05.323
He took Lucas out swimming.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.808
Lucas was on a floating wooden
platform when Chris drowned,

00:10:09.106 --> 00:10:10.252
Two hours,

00:10:10.692 --> 00:10:12.545
Before the kid got rescued.

00:10:16.264 --> 00:10:18.305
Maybe we have an eyewitness after all.

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:20.613
No wonder that kid was so freaked out.

00:10:21.936 --> 00:10:24.573
Watching one of your parents die
isn't something you just get over.

00:10:26.756 --> 00:10:28.012
Can we join you?

00:10:32.017 --> 00:10:33.446
I'm here with my son.

00:10:36.853 --> 00:10:38.093
Mind if I say hi?

00:10:40.455 --> 00:10:43.892
Tell your friend this whole "jerry
maguire" thing's not gonna work on me.

00:10:44.709 --> 00:10:46.389
I don't think that's what this is about.

00:10:49.691 --> 00:10:50.837
How's it going?

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.563
Oh, I used to love these things.

00:11:07.254 --> 00:11:09.217
So crayons is more your thing?

00:11:09.751 --> 00:11:11.744
That's cool. Chicks dig artists.

00:11:14.208 --> 00:11:15.573
Hey, these are pretty good.

00:11:17.159 --> 00:11:19.231
You mind if I sit and
draw with you for a while?

00:11:19.675 --> 00:11:21.261
I'm not so bad myself.

00:11:30.803 --> 00:11:32.671
You know, I'm thinking you can hear me.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.649
You just don't want to talk.

00:11:35.199 --> 00:11:37.396
I don't know exactly
what happened to your dad,

00:11:38.502 --> 00:11:40.372
But I know it was something real bad.

00:11:43.888 --> 00:11:45.473
I think I know how you feel.

00:11:47.938 --> 00:11:50.229
When I was your age, I saw something.

00:11:57.136 --> 00:11:58.329
Anyway . . .

00:12:00.343 --> 00:12:03.169
Maybe you don't think
anyone will listen to you.

00:12:03.912 --> 00:12:04.901
Or, uh...

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.927
Or believe you.

00:12:08.539 --> 00:12:10.313
I want you to know that I will.

00:12:11.726 --> 00:12:13.248
You don't even have to

00:12:13.342 --> 00:12:15.320
Say anything. You
could draw me a picture,

00:12:15.383 --> 00:12:16.734
About what you saw that day,

00:12:17.033 --> 00:12:18.273
With your dad,

00:12:19.575 --> 00:12:20.439
On the lake.

00:12:24.537 --> 00:12:25.448
Okay,

00:12:25.574 --> 00:12:26.562
No problem.

00:12:27.034 --> 00:12:28.054
This is for you.

00:12:29.184 --> 00:12:30.502
This is my family.

00:12:31.806 --> 00:12:33.046
That's my dad.

00:12:33.412 --> 00:12:34.259
That's...

00:12:35.971 --> 00:12:37.006
That's my mom.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.381
That's my geek brother,

00:12:40.276 --> 00:12:41.469
And that's me.

00:12:45.379 --> 00:12:47.073
All right, so I'm a sucky artist.

00:12:47.502 --> 00:12:48.867
I'll see you around, Lucas.

00:13:02.118 --> 00:13:05.069
Lucas hasn't said a
word, not even to me,

00:13:05.686 --> 00:13:06.786
Not since

00:13:07.743 --> 00:13:09.329
His dad's accident.

00:13:10.004 --> 00:13:11.150
Yeah, we heard.

00:13:11.433 --> 00:13:12.359
Sorry.

00:13:13.489 --> 00:13:15.294
What are the doctors saying?

00:13:15.412 --> 00:13:18.080
That it's a kind of
post-Traumatic stress.

00:13:18.174 --> 00:13:19.400
That can't be easy

00:13:19.556 --> 00:13:20.262
For either of you.

00:13:20.326 --> 00:13:21.833
We moved in with my dad.

00:13:22.806 --> 00:13:24.470
He helps out a lot.

00:13:26.471 --> 00:13:27.617
It's just...

00:13:29.203 --> 00:13:32.562
When I think about what Lucas
went through, what he saw...

00:13:34.917 --> 00:13:36.188
Kids are strong.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.775
You'd be surprised
what they can deal with.

00:13:39.576 --> 00:13:40.643
You know,

00:13:41.162 --> 00:13:42.778
He used to have such life.

00:13:43.061 --> 00:13:45.463
He was hard to keep up
with, to tell you the truth.

00:13:46.667 --> 00:13:48.063
Now he just sits there,

00:13:48.174 --> 00:13:50.795
Drawing those pictures,
playing with those army men.

00:13:51.193 --> 00:13:52.339
I just wish.

00:13:53.029 --> 00:13:54.128
Hey, sweetie.

00:13:59.659 --> 00:14:00.444
Thanks.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:02.610
Thanks, Lucas.

00:14:20.788 --> 00:14:22.044
Hey, dad.

00:14:23.441 --> 00:14:25.262
You should probably eat something.

00:14:27.417 --> 00:14:28.988
I'm gonna make some dinner, okay?

00:16:23.954 --> 00:16:25.021
So,

00:16:25.132 --> 00:16:27.157
I think it's safe to say
we can rule out Nessie.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:27.988
What do you mean?

00:16:28.072 --> 00:16:31.211
I just drove past the Carlton
house. There was an ambulance there.

00:16:31.415 --> 00:16:32.766
Will Carlton is dead.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:33.581
He drowned?

00:16:33.628 --> 00:16:35.246
Yep, in the sink.

00:16:35.967 --> 00:16:37.113
What the hell?

00:16:37.494 --> 00:16:39.740
So this isn't a creature. We're
dealing with something else.

00:16:39.787 --> 00:16:40.572
Yeah, but what?

00:16:40.619 --> 00:16:41.231
I don't know.

00:16:41.357 --> 00:16:42.502
A water wraith maybe?

00:16:42.738 --> 00:16:43.821
Some kind of demon?

00:16:44.034 --> 00:16:45.713
I mean, something that controls water

00:16:48.152 --> 00:16:49.707
water that comes from the Same source.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:50.586
The lake Yeah

00:16:50.618 --> 00:16:52.532
Which would explain why
it's upping the body count.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:55.813
The lake is draining. It'll be dry in
a few months. Whatever this thing is,

00:16:55.886 --> 00:16:57.329
Whatever it wants,

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.522
It's running out of time.

00:16:58.555 --> 00:17:00.109
And if it can get through the pipes,

00:17:00.548 --> 00:17:01.558
It can get to anyone,

00:17:01.621 --> 00:17:02.562
Almost anywhere.

00:17:02.656 --> 00:17:04.666
This is gonna happen again soon.

00:17:04.948 --> 00:17:06.455
And we do know one other thing for sure.

00:17:06.487 --> 00:17:08.795
We know this has got something
to do with Bill Carlton.

00:17:08.857 --> 00:17:09.885
It took both his kids.

00:17:09.932 --> 00:17:11.187
And I've been asking around.

00:17:11.313 --> 00:17:12.553
Lucas' dad, Chris

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.327
Bill Carlton's godson.

00:17:15.002 --> 00:17:16.760
Let's go pay Mr. Carlton a visit.

00:17:19.281 --> 00:17:20.552
Mr. Carlton?

00:17:23.283 --> 00:17:25.308
We'd like to ask you a few questions,

00:17:25.387 --> 00:17:26.078
If you don't mind.

00:17:26.141 --> 00:17:28.542
We're from the department I
don't care who you're with.

00:17:29.159 --> 00:17:31.671
I've answered enough questions today.

00:17:33.758 --> 00:17:36.506
Your son said he saw
something in that lake.

00:17:37.479 --> 00:17:38.641
What about you?

00:17:39.181 --> 00:17:40.751
You ever see anything out there?

00:17:42.242 --> 00:17:43.215
Mr. Carlton,

00:17:43.247 --> 00:17:45.209
Sophie's drowning and Will's death.

00:17:45.507 --> 00:17:46.983
We think there might be a connection,

00:17:47.077 --> 00:17:49.981
To you or your family.
My children are gone.

00:17:53.578 --> 00:17:54.348
It's...

00:17:57.503 --> 00:17:59.182
It's worse than dying.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.496
Go away...

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:10.039
Please.

00:18:13.042 --> 00:18:14.282
What do you think?

00:18:15.256 --> 00:18:17.264
I think the poor guy's
been through hell.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.870
I also think he's not
telling us something.

00:18:19.902 --> 00:18:20.923
So now what?

00:18:23.732 --> 00:18:24.642
What is it?

00:18:28.363 --> 00:18:30.985
Maybe Bill's not the only
one who knows something.

00:18:41.748 --> 00:18:43.537
I'm sorry, but I don't
think it's a good idea.

00:18:43.637 --> 00:18:44.736
I just need to talk to him,

00:18:44.799 --> 00:18:45.867
Just for a few minutes.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.656
He won't say anything.

00:18:48.143 --> 00:18:49.775
What good's it gonna do? Andrea,

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:51.596
We think more people might get hurt.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:54.552
We think something's
happening out there.

00:18:54.662 --> 00:18:57.300
My husband, the others,
they just drowned.

00:18:57.723 --> 00:18:58.445
That's all.

00:18:58.493 --> 00:18:59.655
If that's what you really believe,

00:18:59.717 --> 00:19:00.486
Then we'll go,

00:19:00.773 --> 00:19:02.751
But if you think there's
even a possibility

00:19:03.065 --> 00:19:04.855
That something else
could be going on here,

00:19:06.457 --> 00:19:07.932
Please let me talk to your son.

00:19:23.403 --> 00:19:24.690
Hey, Lucas.

00:19:26.217 --> 00:19:27.348
You remember me?

00:19:36.635 --> 00:19:38.190
You know, I, uh...

00:19:39.964 --> 00:19:42.271
I wanted to thank you
for that last drawing

00:19:45.437 --> 00:19:47.101
but the thing is

00:19:47.587 --> 00:19:48.969
I need your help again.

00:20:01.983 --> 00:20:03.632
How did you know to draw this?

00:20:06.619 --> 00:20:08.738
Did you know something
bad was gonna happen?

00:20:10.842 --> 00:20:11.894
Maybe you could

00:20:12.317 --> 00:20:13.855
Nod yes or no

00:20:13.949 --> 00:20:14.781
For me.

00:20:17.262 --> 00:20:18.313
You're scared.

00:20:23.507 --> 00:20:24.371
It's okay.

00:20:25.202 --> 00:20:26.379
I understand.

00:20:26.898 --> 00:20:28.264
See, when I was your age,

00:20:28.342 --> 00:20:30.838
I saw something real
bad happen to my mom,

00:20:33.606 --> 00:20:35.003
And I was scared, too.

00:20:37.802 --> 00:20:39.215
I didn't feel like talking,

00:20:39.607 --> 00:20:40.753
Just like you,

00:20:41.946 --> 00:20:43.500
But, see, my mom,

00:20:45.917 --> 00:20:47.989
I know she wanted me to be brave.

00:20:51.323 --> 00:20:52.986
I think about that every day.

00:20:58.186 --> 00:21:00.180
And I do my best to be brave.

00:21:04.172 --> 00:21:05.783
And maybe your dad

00:21:07.899 --> 00:21:09.500
Wants you to be brave, too.

00:21:31.535 --> 00:21:32.697
Thanks, Lucas.

00:21:37.584 --> 00:21:40.032
Andrea said the kid never drew
like that till his dad died.

00:21:40.126 --> 00:21:43.455
There are cases going
through a traumatic experience

00:21:43.643 --> 00:21:48.310
Could make certain people more sensitive
to premonitions, psychic tendencies.

00:21:48.321 --> 00:21:50.699
What if Lucas is
tapping into it somehow?

00:21:50.992 --> 00:21:52.970
It's only a matter of time
before somebody else drowns,

00:21:52.984 --> 00:21:54.648
So if you got a better lead, please.

00:21:55.406 --> 00:21:56.411
All right.

00:21:56.651 --> 00:21:57.610
We got another house to find.

00:21:57.626 --> 00:22:01.063
There's about a thousand yellow
two-Stories in this county alone.

00:22:01.691 --> 00:22:02.900
See this church?

00:22:03.356 --> 00:22:05.397
I bet there's less than a
thousand of those around here.

00:22:06.203 --> 00:22:08.996
Oh, college boy thinks he's so smart.

00:22:16.382 --> 00:22:17.732
You know, um...

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:20.981
What you said about mom.

00:22:23.996 --> 00:22:25.754
You never told me that before.

00:22:26.303 --> 00:22:27.560
It's no big deal.

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:34.298
Oh, god, we're not gonna have
to hug or anything, are we?

00:23:00.789 --> 00:23:02.437
We're sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:04.918
But does a little boy
live here by chance?

00:23:05.059 --> 00:23:06.064
He might wear

00:23:06.189 --> 00:23:07.273
A blue ball cap,

00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:08.905
Has a red bicycle.

00:23:09.777 --> 00:23:10.829
No, sir.

00:23:12.289 --> 00:23:14.564
Not for a very long time.

00:23:16.119 --> 00:23:18.882
Peter's been gone 35 years now.

00:23:21.831 --> 00:23:23.543
The police never

00:23:24.704 --> 00:23:27.514
I never had any idea what happened.

00:23:30.734 --> 00:23:32.760
He just disappeared.

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:34.806
Losing him,

00:23:36.988 --> 00:23:37.929
You know,

00:23:39.428 --> 00:23:40.009
It's...

00:23:42.150 --> 00:23:44.017
It's worse than dying.

00:23:49.061 --> 00:23:50.820
Did he disappear from here,

00:23:50.882 --> 00:23:51.871
I mean, from this house?

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:53.159
He was supposed to

00:23:54.007 --> 00:23:55.136
Ride his bike

00:23:55.403 --> 00:23:56.565
Straight home

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.773
After school,

00:23:58.198 --> 00:23:59.720
And he never showed up.

00:24:16.751 --> 00:24:18.682
"Peter Sweeney and Billy Carlton,

00:24:18.954 --> 00:24:20.414
1970."

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:27.515
You've taken everything,

00:24:30.042 --> 00:24:31.299
Everyone.

00:24:34.270 --> 00:24:35.573
I've got nothing left.

00:24:39.042 --> 00:24:40.518
I didn't understand.

00:24:42.704 --> 00:24:44.007
I didn't believe.

00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:48.230
Now I think I do.

00:24:50.638 --> 00:24:52.694
I think I finally know what you want.

00:24:57.785 --> 00:24:59.998
Okay, this little boy,
Peter Sweeney, vanishes,

00:25:00.046 --> 00:25:02.400
And this is all connected
to Bill Carlton somehow.

00:25:02.432 --> 00:25:04.362
Bill sure as hell seems
to be hiding something.

00:25:04.425 --> 00:25:05.853
And Bill, the people he loves

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:06.848
They're all getting punished.

00:25:07.052 --> 00:25:08.465
So that Bill did something to Peter.

00:25:08.685 --> 00:25:09.815
What if Bill killed him?

00:25:10.317 --> 00:25:11.667
Peter's spirit would be furious.

00:25:11.746 --> 00:25:13.190
It'd want revenge. It's possible.

00:25:18.622 --> 00:25:20.177
Mr. Carlton!

00:25:23.316 --> 00:25:24.744
Hey. Check it out.

00:25:32.671 --> 00:25:34.837
Mr. Carlton! You need to come back!

00:25:36.046 --> 00:25:38.260
Come out of the water !
Turn the boat around!

00:25:52.111 --> 00:25:53.634
Baby, what's wrong?

00:25:56.774 --> 00:25:58.343
Sam, Dean.

00:25:59.165 --> 00:26:01.065
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:26:02.054 --> 00:26:03.968
So now you're on a first-Name basis.

00:26:05.099 --> 00:26:06.245
What are you doing here?

00:26:06.297 --> 00:26:07.505
I brought you dinner.

00:26:07.852 --> 00:26:10.771
I'm sorry, sweetheart. I
don't really have the time.

00:26:14.905 --> 00:26:16.616
I heard about Bill Carlton.

00:26:16.914 --> 00:26:19.285
Is it true? Is something
going on with the lake?

00:26:21.263 --> 00:26:23.037
Right now, we don't
know what the truth is,

00:26:23.304 --> 00:26:25.800
But I think it might be better
if you and lucas went on home.

00:26:28.745 --> 00:26:30.472
Lucas, hey, what is it?

00:26:30.723 --> 00:26:32.121
Lucas. Lucas.

00:26:32.371 --> 00:26:34.773
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay. Hey,

00:26:34.852 --> 00:26:37.304
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay.

00:26:59.832 --> 00:27:02.972
Okay, just so I'm clear, you see . . .

00:27:03.207 --> 00:27:04.133
Something

00:27:04.619 --> 00:27:06.158
Attack Bill's boat,

00:27:06.629 --> 00:27:07.838
Sending Bill,

00:27:09.246 --> 00:27:11.663
Who is a very good swimmer, by the way,

00:27:11.930 --> 00:27:13.217
Into the drink,

00:27:14.049 --> 00:27:15.776
And you never see him again?

00:27:18.145 --> 00:27:19.683
Yeah, that about sums it up.

00:27:19.730 --> 00:27:21.237
And I'm supposed to believe this,

00:27:21.285 --> 00:27:24.016
Even though I've already
sonar-Swept that entire lake

00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:26.732
And what you're describing is impossible

00:27:27.422 --> 00:27:29.729
And you're not really wildlife service?

00:27:31.020 --> 00:27:31.852
That's right,

00:27:32.103 --> 00:27:32.809
I checked.

00:27:33.092 --> 00:27:34.725
The department's never heard of you two.

00:27:35.233 --> 00:27:35.939
See?

00:27:36.033 --> 00:27:37.948
Now, we can explain that. Enough,

00:27:38.701 --> 00:27:39.785
Please.

00:27:40.931 --> 00:27:43.317
The only reason you're
breathing free air

00:27:43.573 --> 00:27:47.435
Is one of Bill's neighbors saw him
steering out that boat just before you did.

00:27:48.172 --> 00:27:48.833
So

00:27:49.067 --> 00:27:50.653
We have a couple of options here.

00:27:50.952 --> 00:27:53.144
I can arrest you for
impersonating government officials

00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:56.776
And hold you as material witnesses
to Bill Carlton's disappearance,

00:27:57.026 --> 00:27:57.842
Or

00:27:58.156 --> 00:28:00.982
We can chalk this all up to a bad day,

00:28:01.254 --> 00:28:02.713
You get into your car,

00:28:02.854 --> 00:28:05.747
You put this town in
your rearview mirror,

00:28:05.760 --> 00:28:08.913
And you don't ever darken my doorstep

00:28:08.972 --> 00:28:09.688
Again!

00:28:12.403 --> 00:28:13.972
Door number two sounds good.

00:28:14.224 --> 00:28:15.731
That's the one I'd pick.

00:28:30.711 --> 00:28:31.715
Baby...

00:28:33.560 --> 00:28:35.098
What are you doing up?

00:28:37.924 --> 00:28:39.666
Come on, let's go to bed.

00:29:01.053 --> 00:29:02.058
Green.

00:29:02.199 --> 00:29:02.890
What?

00:29:03.015 --> 00:29:04.413
Light's green.

00:29:11.716 --> 00:29:13.554
Ah, the interstate's the other way.

00:29:13.585 --> 00:29:14.197
I know.

00:29:38.568 --> 00:29:41.001
But, Dean, this job, I think it's over.

00:29:41.049 --> 00:29:41.895
I'm not so sure.

00:29:41.943 --> 00:29:44.973
If bill murdered Peter Sweeney
and Peter's spirit got its revenge,

00:29:45.129 --> 00:29:47.233
Case closed. The spirit
should be at rest.

00:29:47.279 --> 00:29:49.602
All right, so what if we take
off and this thing isn't done?

00:29:49.900 --> 00:29:51.931
What if we missed something?
What if more people get hurt?

00:29:52.010 --> 00:29:53.595
But why would you think that?

00:29:55.415 --> 00:29:57.095
Because Lucas was really scared.

00:29:57.362 --> 00:29:58.854
That's what this is about?

00:29:59.827 --> 00:30:02.166
I just don't want to leave
town till I know the kid's okay.

00:30:02.636 --> 00:30:03.626
Who are you,

00:30:03.735 --> 00:30:05.572
And what have you done with my brother?

00:30:07.957 --> 00:30:09.167
Shut up.

00:31:39.810 --> 00:31:41.270
Are you sure about this?

00:31:41.599 --> 00:31:42.902
It's pretty late, man.

00:31:46.234 --> 00:31:47.710
Lucas? Lucas!

00:31:50.661 --> 00:31:51.587
Lucas!

00:32:30.791 --> 00:32:31.858
Can you tell me?

00:32:33.998 --> 00:32:34.862
No

00:32:42.933 --> 00:32:44.644
It doesn't make any sense.

00:32:48.756 --> 00:32:50.295
I'm going crazy.

00:32:51.315 --> 00:32:52.839
No, you're not.

00:32:54.268 --> 00:32:55.446
Tell me what happened.

00:32:56.058 --> 00:32:57.000
Everything.

00:33:01.204 --> 00:33:02.334
I heard...

00:33:05.317 --> 00:33:07.060
I thought I heard...

00:33:09.376 --> 00:33:11.197
There was this voice.

00:33:11.715 --> 00:33:12.688
What did it say?

00:33:12.735 --> 00:33:13.583
It said

00:33:14.547 --> 00:33:16.807
It said, "come play with me."

00:33:24.826 --> 00:33:26.333
What's happening?

00:33:45.689 --> 00:33:47.510
Do you recognize the
kids in these pictures?

00:33:47.635 --> 00:33:48.389
What?

00:33:50.304 --> 00:33:51.199
No, I huh...

00:33:51.278 --> 00:33:54.401
I mean, except that's
my dad right there.

00:33:54.610 --> 00:33:55.975
He must have been about

00:33:56.588 --> 00:33:58.220
12 in these pictures.

00:33:59.855 --> 00:34:01.220
Chris Bar's drowning

00:34:01.502 --> 00:34:03.873
The connection wasn't to Bill
Carlton. It must have been to sheriff.

00:34:03.935 --> 00:34:05.395
Bill and the sheriff,

00:34:05.756 --> 00:34:07.374
They were both involved with Peter.

00:34:07.646 --> 00:34:08.676
What about Chris?

00:34:09.293 --> 00:34:11.460
My dad, what are you talking about?

00:34:11.696 --> 00:34:12.591
Lucas?

00:34:13.313 --> 00:34:14.646
Lucas, what is it?

00:34:20.975 --> 00:34:23.157
Lucas, honey?

00:34:34.954 --> 00:34:37.402
You and Lucas get back to the
house and stay there, okay?

00:35:01.787 --> 00:35:03.043
Peter's bike.

00:35:03.844 --> 00:35:04.895
Who are you?

00:35:08.302 --> 00:35:09.793
Put the gun down, Jake.

00:35:10.499 --> 00:35:11.979
How did you know that was there?

00:35:12.026 --> 00:35:12.874
What happened?

00:35:13.079 --> 00:35:14.632
You and Bill killed Peter,

00:35:14.978 --> 00:35:16.830
Drowned him in the lake,
and then buried the bike?

00:35:17.788 --> 00:35:19.515
You can't bury the truth, Jake.

00:35:20.698 --> 00:35:22.330
Nothing stays buried.

00:35:25.909 --> 00:35:27.416
Go to your room, sweetie.

00:35:28.704 --> 00:35:29.551
Now.

00:35:29.599 --> 00:35:31.877
Lock the door and wait
for me. Don't come out.

00:35:32.253 --> 00:35:33.618
I don't know what the
hell you're talking about.

00:35:33.640 --> 00:35:36.067
You and Bill killed Peter
Sweeney 35 years ago.

00:35:36.162 --> 00:35:37.083
That's what the hell I'm talking about.

00:35:37.088 --> 00:35:37.700
Dad

00:35:37.982 --> 00:35:40.070
And now you got one
seriously pissed-Off spirit.

00:35:40.117 --> 00:35:41.373
It's gonna take Andrea,

00:35:41.483 --> 00:35:42.267
Lucas,

00:35:42.568 --> 00:35:43.557
Everyone you love.

00:35:44.059 --> 00:35:45.143
It's gonna drown them,

00:35:45.550 --> 00:35:47.419
And it's gonna drag their
bodies god knows where.

00:35:47.717 --> 00:35:49.993
So you can feel the Same
pain Peter's mom felt.

00:35:50.857 --> 00:35:52.160
And then after that,

00:35:53.053 --> 00:35:54.105
It's gonna take you,

00:35:54.419 --> 00:35:56.146
And it's not gonna stop until it does.

00:35:57.040 --> 00:35:58.108
How do you know that?

00:35:58.218 --> 00:36:00.683
Because that's exactly
what it did to Bill Carlton.

00:36:00.730 --> 00:36:01.879
Listen to yourselves,

00:36:02.130 --> 00:36:02.743
Both of you.

00:36:02.805 --> 00:36:03.936
You're insane.

00:36:03.983 --> 00:36:06.180
I don't really give a rat's
ass what you think of us,

00:36:07.192 --> 00:36:08.840
But if we're gonna
bring down this spirit,

00:36:09.060 --> 00:36:10.614
We need to find the remains,

00:36:10.881 --> 00:36:11.697
Salt them,

00:36:11.838 --> 00:36:12.969
And burn them into dust.

00:36:13.173 --> 00:36:14.690
Tell me you buried Peter somewhere.

00:36:14.712 --> 00:36:16.449
Tell me you didn't just
let him go in the lake.

00:36:21.834 --> 00:36:24.534
Come play with me.

00:36:28.416 --> 00:36:28.981
Dad,

00:36:29.044 --> 00:36:30.080
Is any of this true?

00:36:30.111 --> 00:36:31.367
No. Don't listen to them.

00:36:31.393 --> 00:36:32.702
They're liars, and they're dangerous.

00:36:32.858 --> 00:36:34.491
Something tried to drown me.

00:36:35.041 --> 00:36:36.328
Chris died on that lake.

00:36:36.359 --> 00:36:37.505
Dad, look at me.

00:36:40.832 --> 00:36:41.506
Tell me you

00:36:41.570 --> 00:36:43.108
You didn't kill anyone.

00:36:53.029 --> 00:36:54.144
Oh, my god.

00:36:58.210 --> 00:36:59.711
Billy and I were at the lake.

00:37:02.803 --> 00:37:05.441
Peter was the smallest
one. We always bullied him,

00:37:05.975 --> 00:37:07.089
But this time...

00:37:08.350 --> 00:37:09.449
It got rough.

00:37:14.394 --> 00:37:16.042
We were holding his
head under the water.

00:37:16.942 --> 00:37:18.198
We didn't mean to,

00:37:19.030 --> 00:37:20.726
But we held him under too long,

00:37:20.851 --> 00:37:22.060
And he drowned.

00:37:29.076 --> 00:37:30.395
We let the body go,

00:37:31.117 --> 00:37:32.185
And it sank.

00:37:39.282 --> 00:37:40.522
Oh, Andrea.

00:37:43.635 --> 00:37:44.813
We were kids.

00:37:45.315 --> 00:37:46.210
We were so scared.

00:37:46.241 --> 00:37:47.261
It was a mistake,

00:37:47.278 --> 00:37:48.135
But, Andrea,

00:37:48.428 --> 00:37:50.846
To say that I have anything
to do with these drownings,

00:37:50.877 --> 00:37:52.008
With Chris,

00:37:52.431 --> 00:37:54.080
Because of some ghost

00:37:54.362 --> 00:37:55.917
It's not rational.

00:37:56.941 --> 00:37:58.212
All right, listen to me,

00:37:58.715 --> 00:37:59.672
All of you.

00:38:00.348 --> 00:38:01.855
We need to get you away from this lake

00:38:01.949 --> 00:38:03.597
As far as we can right now.

00:38:07.535 --> 00:38:08.115
Lucas!

00:38:11.951 --> 00:38:14.007
Come play with me.

00:38:14.918 --> 00:38:15.703
Lucas!

00:38:15.895 --> 00:38:18.595
Lucas! Stay where you are!

00:38:37.648 --> 00:38:38.746
Oh, my god!

00:38:42.231 --> 00:38:43.424
Andrea, stay there.

00:38:43.566 --> 00:38:44.649
No, Lucas!

00:38:44.701 --> 00:38:46.004
We'll get him. Stay on the dock.

00:38:52.311 --> 00:38:53.289
Lucas?

00:38:56.017 --> 00:38:56.817
Sam?

00:38:58.717 --> 00:39:00.271
Lucas, where are you?

00:39:04.562 --> 00:39:05.190
Peter,

00:39:05.362 --> 00:39:06.336
If you can hear me,

00:39:07.501 --> 00:39:08.443
Please, Peter,

00:39:08.475 --> 00:39:09.228
I'm sorry.

00:39:10.719 --> 00:39:11.551
I'm so... Dad, no!

00:39:11.598 --> 00:39:12.666
I'm so sorry.

00:39:13.169 --> 00:39:13.734
Peter.

00:39:13.969 --> 00:39:14.660
Lucas

00:39:14.958 --> 00:39:17.124
He's j... he's just a little boy.

00:39:17.835 --> 00:39:19.923
Please, it's not his fault. It's mine.

00:39:20.065 --> 00:39:21.242
Please take me!

00:39:22.246 --> 00:39:22.796
Jake,

00:39:22.858 --> 00:39:23.220
No!

00:39:24.523 --> 00:39:25.983
Listen, let it be over!

00:39:28.252 --> 00:39:28.942
Dad

00:39:29.777 --> 00:39:30.610
Daddy!

00:39:33.152 --> 00:39:34.015
No

00:39:44.043 --> 00:39:44.906
No...

00:40:25.434 --> 00:40:26.172
Look,

00:40:27.004 --> 00:40:28.386
We're not gonna save everybody.

00:40:31.028 --> 00:40:31.687
I know.

00:40:32.471 --> 00:40:33.225
Sam,

00:40:33.602 --> 00:40:34.293
Dean.

00:40:34.434 --> 00:40:35.203
Hey.

00:40:36.929 --> 00:40:38.091
We're glad we caught you.

00:40:38.531 --> 00:40:39.426
We just, um,

00:40:40.623 --> 00:40:42.130
We made you lunch for the road.

00:40:42.915 --> 00:40:45.662
Lucas insisted on making
the sandwiches himself.

00:40:47.142 --> 00:40:48.194
Can I give it to them now?

00:40:50.125 --> 00:40:50.737
Of course.

00:40:51.960 --> 00:40:53.781
Come on, Lucas, let's
load this in the car.

00:41:00.426 --> 00:41:01.367
How you holding up?

00:41:03.816 --> 00:41:06.752
It's just gonna take a long time to
sort through everything, you know?

00:41:10.713 --> 00:41:12.314
Andrea, I'm sorry.

00:41:13.914 --> 00:41:15.123
You saved my son.

00:41:16.913 --> 00:41:18.655
I can't ask for more than that.

00:41:22.343 --> 00:41:23.207
Dad loved me.

00:41:24.337 --> 00:41:25.593
He loved Lucas.

00:41:26.582 --> 00:41:27.587
No matter what he did,

00:41:27.608 --> 00:41:28.732
I just have to...

00:41:30.495 --> 00:41:31.548
Hold on to that.

00:41:37.766 --> 00:41:38.587
All right,

00:41:38.750 --> 00:41:40.226
If you're gonna be talking now,

00:41:40.522 --> 00:41:43.540
This is a very important phrase, so
I want you to repeat it one more time.

00:41:43.737 --> 00:41:44.694
Zeppelin rules!

00:41:44.698 --> 00:41:46.109
That's right. Up high.

00:41:49.808 --> 00:41:51.774
Take care of your mom, okay?

00:41:59.746 --> 00:42:01.288
Thank you.

00:42:06.482 --> 00:42:07.761
Sam, move your ass.

00:42:08.156 --> 00:42:10.223
We're gonna run out of
daylight before we hit the road.

00:00:00.006 --> 00:00:01.511
